<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past month.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in past month.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest rising and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the month to July 11.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in month	  Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     change</p>
<p> 1   Macquarie Bank	   12.85	26.85</p>
<p> 2   Burns,Philp &amp; Co	  2.41	19.90</p>
<p> 3   Commonwealth BK	  16.36	14.41</p>
<p> 4   Publish Broadcst	  7.96	14.04</p>
<p> 5   Fletcher-Energy div     4.38	13.02</p>
<p> 6   National Mutual	   2.15	12.57</p>
<p> 7   Jupiters Ltd		3.45	12.38</p>
<p> 8   Westfield Amer T	  1.20	12.37</p>
<p> 9   Westpac Bkg		 8.10	11.11</p>
<p>10   Transurban Group     1115.00	10.95</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in month	    Percent</p>
<p>Rank Name			  Price     change</p>
<p> 1   Acacia Resources	  1.39     -27.60</p>
<p> 2   Newcrest Mining	   2.50     -25.82</p>
<p> 3   Centaur Min&amp;Expl	  1.25     -22.84</p>
<p> 4   Plutonic Rsc		3.81     -21.44</p>
<p> 5   Goldfields		  1.70     -20.93</p>
<p> 6   Sthn Pac Pete	     3.90     -17.89</p>
<p> 7   Lihir Gold		  1.90     -17.03</p>
<p> 8   RGC			   4.36     -15.34</p>
<p> 9   Great Central	     2.26     -12.06</p>
<p>10   Sons Of Gwalia	    4.88	-8.79</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
